WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.468
-My next guest is
the Oscar-nominated star

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.571
of "Goodfellas"
and the Emmy-nominated star

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.871
of "The Sopranos."

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.140
She is awesome.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.343
She now has an awesome new show
for HGTV called

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.946
"My Big Italian Adventure,"
and I think it's the best idea.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:17.183
It airs its finale
this Friday at 9:00 p.m.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.218
Here is Lorraine Bracco.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:22.021
Lorraine, look at you.
You look great, buddy.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.457
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.524
I appreciate this.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.594
-I love coming on your show,
Jimmy.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.761
It's always fun.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.363
-I heard that you're in Memphis

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.732
now working a new movie,
is that right?

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.936
-Yep. I am in Memphis, and I
went to Graceland yesterday.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.804
-I've never been. How was it?

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:40.773
-It was on my bucket list.

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.208
-Me too.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.843
-Oh, my God.
-I love Elvis.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.012
-You got to get Dee Dee
to give you --

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.381
She gave me a private tour.
-Dee Dee.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.651
-She was phenomenal.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:55.454
-Did you just --
I'm freaking out. I love Elvis.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.356
-She told me
so many great stories.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:01.327
One of the great stories that
I loved was Bruce Springsteen,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:05.465
when he was starting out,
he climbed over the wall,

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.134
and security went and got him,
and he said,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.536
"Look, I'm Bruce Springsteen.
I'm a singer."

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.005
Yeah, like,
"No, you're out of here."

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:16.075
-[ Laughs ] It's like not yet,
you're not Bruce Springsteen.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.344
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.679
-You're almost
Bruce Springsteen.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.281
Yeah, get out of here.
Yeah, this is Elvis' house.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.684
But wait, did you see
the Jungle Room and everything?

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:28.120
-Everything, everything!
-Ah.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.189
-It was phenomenal.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:34.227
Jimmy, it is so worth
everything.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.429
I mean, look, if you love Elvis,
forget it.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.863
-I love Elvis.
-Which I do.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.498
Did you see my new shirt?

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.167
-I mean, I was looking at that.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.803
I said, "Oh, my goodness,
come on."

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.038
That is gorgeous!

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:47.506
-I love it.
-I love it.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:48.875
I want to talk to you
about so many things.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.175
I want to talk to you
about the show.

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:51.411
I think it's perfect.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.912
I think you set it up perfectly.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.947
It's perfect on brand for you.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:58.851
'Cause I see you and honestly,
I go right to "Goodfellas"

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.921
or I go to "Sopranos"
and I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.356
You must be like, "Yeah, I know.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.691
Yeah, I was in 'The Sopranos.'
Yes, I was in 'Goodfellas.'"

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:09.062
But you were
in two legendary things.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.197
I mean --
-I was lucky.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.432
-Ah, no way.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.500
Have you --
Do you ever watch your stuff?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.536
Or are you an actor
that doesn't watch their work?

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.906
-I don't really watch my stuff.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.676
But I know a lot of people --
I know it was like the 30th year

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.512
of "Goodfellas,"
which I can't even believe

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.981
because I still feel
like I'm 12.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:35.187
But one of the things I did do
was I saw the film

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:42.895
in its entirety at
the Hollywood Forever Cemetery.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.164
-Oh, I've never been there!
I've heard about that.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:46.832
-That's another bucket list.

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.535
I'm going through my bucket list
really quickly.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.938
Jimmy, you got to get --
-It's like a drive-in, right?

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.906
Or a picnic or something?
-No.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:58.978
It's a picnic,
and there were 4,000 people

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.113
that came to watch "Goodfellas."

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:05.217
It was a full moon, and I
watched it with an audience,

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.587
which is what I had
always wanted to do.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:10.156
-Did anyone know you were there?

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.992
-The people knew,
you know, who run

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.295
the Hollywood Cemetery thing
knew me.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:17.864
But no, no, I did.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.199
I gave a little speech
in the beginning,

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.702
and people were, like, crazy.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.071
-See, come on, that's what
it's all about, right?

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:28.207
I mean, I don't know.
I think of you.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.509
You know how many people,
like -- even when I make

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:34.013
Italian food, I'll throw on
"Goodfellas" or just --

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.749
It just gets me in the mood,
and you go, "Yeah."

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.084
So that's when I heard about
your show.

00:03:39.084 --> 00:03:43.022
I go, "Oh, this is
the most genius idea."

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:48.561
Explain to me how you heard
about this house for sale.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:55.601
-So, my phone, I get those
alerts and CNN writes, you know,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:59.138
buy a 1-euro house in Sicily.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.474
And I'm like, "Yeah, okay."
-Yeah.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.443
-You know, let me sell you
a bridge, okay?

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:09.916
So I press on it and I read all
about the mayor and the town

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:14.186
and the people, and, you know,
how they need to revitalize

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:17.790
this town and that they have
some houses.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.260
I just thought --
I went to sleep and I got up

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.829
the next morning and I said,

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:26.465
"You know, this is a great show
for HGTV."

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:28.601
-Yep.
-"This is a good idea."

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.404
They said, "Lorraine, if you
want to do it, it's yours."

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:34.040
And I was thinking more of
maybe it could be something

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.909
I could produce for somebody.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.978
-Yeah, you go,
"Wait, I don't have to be in it.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.447
I have to do the renovating."

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:44.049
-I wasn't thinking about me.

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:47.686
So the fun part about it was is
they were so cool.

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:49.989
They said, "Listen, we're going
to send you over.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.957
If you love it, we'll do it.

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:55.028
If you don't love it, meh, meh.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.697
We'll let it go."
-Yeah.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:03.169
-So, of course, I go over,
and my first vision of the town

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:07.540
is this gorgeous hillside, and I
look out, and there's rolling,

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:13.913
beautiful wheat fields
and vineyards and olive groves.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:20.520
And then I see the shepherd with
his 100 sheep cross the road.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.622
-I mean, I'm weeping.
I'm weeping already.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.956
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.691
-Sold!
-And I started to laugh.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:28.594
I said, "Oh, my God,
this could only happen to me.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.663
This is fantastic."

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.031
-It seems too good to be true.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.100
You go, one euro,
which is, like $1.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.403
You bought a house in Sicily.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:41.273
But then you get there
and how is the place?

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:42.775
-It's a [bleep]hole.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:46.612
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.880
It's a disaster!

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.550
-It's worse than that.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.552
It's a dirt floor.

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:56.822
It's caving-in rock walls

00:05:56.822 --> 00:06:00.059
that are, you know,
huge and enormous.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.527
You can't move them.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.995
There's no roof.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.797
That's not true.
There was a roof.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.732
It was bamboo.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.767
Bamboo and a couple of leaves.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.903
-Oh, my God,
you're like, one euro.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:14.774
Now you owe them money
from buying the place.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:19.812
-There's no plumbing,
no electricity.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.849
Yeah, there was --
it was a [bleep]hole.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:26.986
-But you -- Well, you have to
watch the show to watch it,

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:30.289
"My Big Italian Adventure,"
but you got to work with

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:33.392
great people and all the locals
and all that stuff, correct?

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.227
-Oh, it was magnificent.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:38.564
I mean, I don't think you could
really build a house like this

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:42.402
here without costing literally
millions of dollars.

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.570
-Wow.
-Everything -- Everything was

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.806
reclaimed, all the doors,
all the windows.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:51.143
-Ah!
-They carved out sinks for me.

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:54.647
I have beautiful stone sinks.
You can't imagine.

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.949
It's to die for.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:59.318
-As soon as quarantine is done,

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.320
you know I have to
stop around there.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.991
I will be calling you, please.
-Come on. Come on.

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:09.695
-Who is the guy that helped you
out, the contractor, was it?

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.965
-Piero.
-Piero.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:16.635
Now, Piero, he knows our show?

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:18.070
-He loves you.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:22.140
-Piero, if you're watching,
buona sera.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.509
[ Italian accent ]
It's me, Jimmy Fallon.

00:07:24.509 --> 00:07:29.815
[ Normal voice ] Your work is
bellissimo, magnifico.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:32.151
Grazie mille.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.253
Is that okay?
-Oh, my God. Yes.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:37.523
And what you should ask him is
when you want to make your house

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:40.259
over there,
you're going to need him.

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.894
-Can you lend me a euro?

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:43.528
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:45.464
-No problem.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:46.798
-I want to show a clip.

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.768
Here's Lorraine Bracco
in "My Big Italian Adventure."

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.037
Take a look at this.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:54.306
-I can't move this,
so we're going to build a block.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:59.411
Like, we'll build around it,
on top of it and make a --

00:07:59.411 --> 00:08:01.647
What do you call that?

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.981 line:0%
A, uh...

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:04.216 line:0%
-The sink.
-Something solid?

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:06.986 line:0%
-No sinks.
-Uh, uh, uh...

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.520
Is it bigger than a bread box?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.655
-Sounds like...

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.990
-Yeah, one word.
-Yes.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.859 line:0%
-Storage?
-No storage.

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.727 line:0%
-A cabinet?
-A countertop.

00:08:15.727 --> 00:08:17.797 line:0%
-Countertop. I'm so sorry.

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:20.399 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.134
-Lorraine Bracco, everybody.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.970
Check out the finale of
"My Big Italian Adventure"

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:28.541
this Friday at 9:00 p.m.
on HGTV.

